# Known bug: a permanent's permission to spend mana as though it were any color is read off its card whether or not it has lost all its abilities (CR 613.1f, 609.4b); `sources` in static_rules.rs never looks at LoseAllAbilities.
# Agatha's Soul Cauldron: "You may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to activate abilities of creatures you control."
# (The control is agathas-soul-cauldron-any-color-mana-is-for-creature-abilities-only.) Bot1 casts it and Blazing Rootwalla on turn 1.
# Bot2's Oko, Thief of Crowns makes the Cauldron an Elk with no abilities on turn 2. On turn 3 the {U} of Mox Sapphire cannot pay for
# Rootwalla's "{R}: +2/+0": the {U} stays in the pool, and Mox Ruby pays.

